# Patent Claim: System for Combined Information and Energy Transmission Across an Isolation Barrier

**What is claimed is:**

**1.** A system for transmitting information concurrently with energy across an isolation barrier separating a transmitter from a galvanically isolated receiver, the system comprising:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a transmitter configured to generate a plurality of discrete energy transfer events across the isolation barrier, each said energy transfer event conveying a quantum of energy to the receiver;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a controller operatively coupled to the transmitter and configured to modulate at least one characteristic of successive energy transfer events in accordance with an input information signal, wherein said modulation is constrained by a minimum event threshold and a maximum event threshold;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;wherein the minimum event threshold defines a lower bound on the occurrence of energy transfer events sufficient to maintain a predetermined energy delivery to the receiver, and the maximum event threshold defines an upper bound on the occurrence of energy transfer events;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;wherein the controller applies a first function f1 to encode a first logical state of the input information signal by regulating the energy transfer events in accordance with the minimum event threshold, and applies a second function f2 to encode a second logical state of the input information signal by regulating the energy transfer events in accordance with the maximum event threshold; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a receiver, galvanically isolated from the transmitter by the isolation barrier, comprising a detector configured to observe said at least one characteristic of the received energy transfer events and to recover the input information signal by discriminating between an output of the first function f1 and an output of the second function f2 relative to the minimum and maximum event thresholds.

**2.** The system of claim 1, wherein said at least one characteristic comprises a count of energy transfer events occurring within a predefined temporal window.

**3.** The system of claim 2, wherein the first function f1 causes the count of energy transfer events within said temporal window to satisfy said minimum event threshold and the second function f2 causes said count to satisfy said maximum event threshold, and wherein the detector recovers a bit value in dependence upon whether the observed count more closely corresponds to the minimum event threshold or the maximum event threshold.

**4.** The system of claim 1, wherein said at least one characteristic comprises at least one of a temporal spacing between successive energy transfer events, an amplitude of an energy transfer event, and a duration of an energy transfer event.

**5.** The system of claim 1, wherein the receiver further comprises an energy storage element configured to accumulate energy from the energy transfer events, and wherein the minimum event threshold is selected such that the accumulated energy does not fall below a level required to sustain operation of the receiver irrespective of the logical states encoded by the input information signal.

**6.** The system of claim 1, wherein each of the first function f1 and the second function f2 comprises a mapping from a symbol of the input information signal to a corresponding number of energy transfer events bounded by, respectively, the minimum event threshold and the maximum event threshold.

**7.** The system of claim 1, wherein the detector comprises a comparator configured to compare the observed characteristic against at least one decision threshold intermediate the minimum event threshold and the maximum event threshold.

**8.** The system of claim 1, wherein the isolation barrier comprises at least one of a transformer, a capacitive coupling, and an optical coupling.

**9.** A method for transmitting information concurrently with energy across an isolation barrier, the method comprising:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;generating, at a transmitter, a plurality of discrete energy transfer events across the isolation barrier to a galvanically isolated receiver;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;receiving an input information signal;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for a first logical state of the input information signal, applying a first function f1 to regulate the energy transfer events in accordance with a minimum event threshold;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for a second logical state of the input information signal, applying a second function f2 to regulate the energy transfer events in accordance with a maximum event threshold;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;wherein the minimum event threshold is selected to maintain a predetermined delivery of energy to the receiver;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;observing, at the receiver, a characteristic of the received energy transfer events; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;recovering the input information signal by discriminating between the first function f1 and the second function f2 relative to the minimum and maximum event thresholds.

**10.** The method of claim 9, further comprising accumulating energy from the received energy transfer events in an energy storage element of the receiver, the minimum event threshold being selected such that a stored energy level of the receiver remains above an operational minimum regardless of which of the first and second logical states is transmitted.

